# Nothing here that signs or unlocks a release may ever be committed.
#
# The upload keystore is the one file in this project that cannot be
# regenerated. See README.md — losing it means you cannot update the app under
# the same listing, and a leaked one means somebody else can.
*.keystore
*.jks
*.p12
*.pepk
keystore.properties
local.properties

# Bubblewrap writes the keystore passwords here after `init`.
.bubblewrap/
bubblewrap.config.json

# Generated by `bubblewrap init` / `update`, and rewritten by apply-config.mjs
# on every build. Untracked on purpose: this file holds whichever host the last
# build targeted, so tracking it means a `git add -A` during preview testing
# silently commits a vercel.app host as the production config. apply-config.mjs
# is the real source of truth — it sets every field that matters, with the
# reasons written down next to each one.
twa-manifest.json
manifest-checksum.txt
store_icon.png

# JVM crash dumps, which Gradle leaves behind when the daemon dies.
hs_err_pid*.log
replay_pid*.log

# Build output. `bubblewrap build` regenerates all of it.
app/
gradle/
gradlew
gradlew.bat
build.gradle
settings.gradle
gradle.properties
/build/
.gradle/
*.apk
*.aab
*.idsig
output.json
assetlinks.json

# The Play service account key, if you ever use `bubblewrap play`.
*-service-account.json
